{"id":"u-0659752d-5ee7-46d5-bb5d-794028c84aa5","src":"community","title":"FOUR AND SEVEN","author":"Kael C.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/gwZdIB-four-and-seven","desc":"In all seriousness, this program is simple, 4 days a week (2 days on, 1 off, 2 on, 2 off)\n\nI'm making this program for the simplest reason. I don't like the strength programs such as 5/3/1 or 5x5 because I feel like I'm doing nothing in these. I want to push hard, not often, but very hard ; simply because my body reacts the best when I use low reps (4) for sets.\nWhen doing accessory work, I won't use this kind of reps, instead I'll go a little bit higher (7), because it feels nice :)\n\n4 main lifts : OHP, Deadlift, Bench, Squat with a mandatory back exercise after each to complement the lifts. After that, one variation of the main lift, then one isolation.\n\nTo avoid a lot of fatigue and to keep the form on point, you will not use your true 1rm, you will use a TM (Training Max) that will be 93% of your 1rm.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-03-15T02:03:56.881Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":4,"pct":88},{"r":4,"pct":92}],"note":"If you can't manage the small percentage difference, use the same weight. Adapt."},{"n":"Chin-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":8.5}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":8.5}]},{"n":"Single Arm Pushdown","sets":[{"r":7,"rpe":8}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":4,"pct":88},{"r":4,"pct":92}]},{"n":"Barbell Row","sets":[{"r":7,"rpe":8.5}]},{"n":"Good Morning","sets":[{"r":7,"rpe":8.5}]},{"n":"Lying Leg Curl","sets":[{"r":7,"rpe":8}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":4,"pct":88},{"r":4,"pct":92}]},{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":8.5}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"r":4,"rpe":8.5}]},{"n"